{
  "text": "2017A02 Compare\nand contrast O2 delivery via nasal cannulae, simple facemask and Venturi mask\nList:\n·\nFirst: describe device, fixed vs variable, max\nFiO\n2\n, flow rate\n·\nSecond: reservoir, dead space, humidification\n·\nThird: sources of error, pros and cons\nNasal cannulae:\nFeatures\n·\nOne\n  short prong in either nostril\n·\nTubing\n  connects to cylinder or wall\n·\nVariable\n  performance device\n·\nGas\n  flow rate 1-4L/min\n·\nFiO\n2\n≤ 0.4\n·\nReservoir\n  in nasopharynx but not device\n·\nNo\n  dead space\n·\nNo\n  humidification\nPros\n·\nSimple\n·\nComfortable\n  at low flow rate\n·\nNo\n  risk of rebreathing\n·\nPatient\n  can eat\nCons\n·\nDrying and epistaxis at high flow rate or\n  prolonged use\nFactors affecting FiO2\n·\n↑\n  Peak inspiratory flow rate (PIFR) -> ↑air entrainment -> ↓ FiO\n2\n·\n↑V\nT\n-> ↑air entrainment\n·\nHence\n  most effective if the cause of hypoxia is hypoventilation\nFace mask:\nFeatures\n·\nMask\n  with ~100mL volume inside\n·\nHoles\n  on the size (sometimes expiratory-opening flap valves)\n·\nTubing\n  from the bottom (sometimes with reservoir bag)\n·\nVariable\n  performance\n·\nGas\n  flow rate up to 10L/min\n·\nFiO\n2\n:\n  up to 0.6 (up to 0.8 if reservoir bag)\n·\nMask\n  is both O\n2\nreservoir and dead space 100mL\n·\n±\nextra reservoir in bag ~500mL?\n·\nNo\n  humidification\nPros\n·\nEasy\n  to use\n·\nComfortable\n·\nCan\n  deliver nebulized medicines e.g. salbutamol\nCons\n·\nLess\n  comfortable\n·\nCan’t\n  eat, can’t talk much\nFactors affecting FiO\n2\n·\nAs for nasal cannulae, but less affected due\n  to reservoir\nVenturi mask:\nFeatures\n·\nWell-fitting\n  face mask\n·\nExhalation\n  pores\n·\nO\n2\nsupply at the bottom, larger bore tubing\n·\nVenturi\n  device within the tubing (see pic)\n·\n100%\n  O\n2\nflows through a constriction\n·\n?\n  Bernoulli principle: ↑kinetic energy -> ↓potential (pressure) energy ->\n  room air entrained due to pressure gradient\n·\n?\n  Coanda effect: air drawn in due to friction and surface tension forces\n  (probably this)\n·\nFixed\n  performance device; specified entrainment ratio for each attachment\n·\nFiO\n2\nup to 0.7 (but less accurate >0.5)\n·\nMask\n  is both O\n2\nreservoir and dead space ~100mL\n·\nHumidifier\n  present\nPros\n·\nFixed\n  performance -> can calculate PAO\n2\n, A-a gradient\n·\nCan\n  be humidified\nCons\n·\nUncomfortable\n·\nCan’t\n  be sure of fixed performance due to leak\nFactors affecting FiO\n2\n·\n↑↑\n  PIFR -> air entrainment around the sides of the mask, becomes a variable\n  performance device\n·\nWater\n  -> obstruction -> ↓entrainment\nFeedback welcome at\nketaminenightmares@gmail.com",
